{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fingering"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFingering","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFingering","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLFingeringV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<fingering>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe\/note-swift.struct\/fingering"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/Note-swift.struct\/fingering"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","title":"fingering","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLFrameV4NoteV9fingeringAA12MXLFingeringVSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fingering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFingering","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLFingeringV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The fingering used for this note.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/Note-swift.struct"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFingering":{"title":"MXLFingering","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFingering"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfingering","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFingering"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFingering","abstract":[{"text":"Fingering is typically indicated 1,2,3,4,5. Multiple fingerings may be given, typically to substitute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingerings in the middle of a note. The substitution and alternate values are “no” if the attribute is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present. For guitar and other fretted instruments, the fingering element represents the fretting finger; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pluck element represents the plucking finger.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The frame type represents a frame or fretboard diagram used together with a chord symbol. The representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is based on the NIFF guitar grid with additional information. The frame type’s unplayed attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what to display above a string that has no associated frame-note element. Typical values are x and the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string. If the attribute is not present, the display of the unplayed string is application-defined.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFrame","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFrame","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame/Note-swift.struct/fingering":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe\/note-swift.struct\/fingering","title":"fingering","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/Note-swift.struct\/fingering","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The fingering used for this note.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fingering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFingering","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLFingeringV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame/Note-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The frame-note type represents each note included in the frame. An open string will have a fret value of 0,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while a muted string will not be associated with a frame-note element.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe\/note-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFrame.Note","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/Note-swift.struct","role":"symbol"}}}